---
import AudienceAside from "../../components/AudienceAside.astro";
import Panel from "../../components/ds/Panel.astro";
import Prose from "../../components/ds/Prose.astro";
import AudienceLanding from "../../layouts/AudienceLanding.astro";

// The service's own content for social workers, word for word as the live site
// has it. The placement-moves inset becomes a design-system advice panel with the
// same words.
---

<AudienceLanding
	audience="social-workers"
	eyebrow="For social workers"
	title="Social workers"
	headline="Your role in the Personal Education Plan"
	lead="How to work with the Virtual School to improve a child's education."
	illustration={{ name: "home", alt: "" }}
	breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Social workers" }]}
	description="Your part in the PEP, how to refer a child, and how we work together to improve outcomes."
>
	<Prose>
		<h2>Your role in the PEP</h2>
		<p>
			The PEP forms part of the child's care plan. It is a shared responsibility between the social
			worker, the school and the Virtual School, and it should be a live document that reflects the
			child's day-to-day experience.
		</p>
		<p>As the social worker, you are responsible for:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>making sure the PEP happens within the statutory timescales</li>
			<li>chairing or attending the PEP meeting, and making sure the child's views are captured</li>
			<li>making sure the PEP links to the wider care plan — health, contact, placement stability</li>
			<li>escalating to the Virtual School when a school is not meeting the child's needs</li>
		</ul>
	</Prose>

	<Panel tone="advice" title="Placement moves and school">
		<p>
			Tell us as early as possible about a placement move. A rushed school move is the single
			biggest cause of lost school time for children in care, and we can usually prevent it if we
			have notice.
		</p>
	</Panel>

	<Prose>
		<h2>Raising a concern</h2>
		<p>
			If you think a child's education is at risk — attendance is dropping, a school is not putting
			the PEP provision in place, or an exclusion is being considered — contact the Virtual School
			directly rather than waiting for the next review.
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				Email the team: <a href="mailto:virtualschool@rotherham.gov.uk">virtualschool@rotherham.gov.uk</a>
			</li>
			<li>See <a href="/our-team/">our team</a> for the phase lead for your child</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Attendance and exclusions</h2>
		<p>
			We monitor attendance and exclusion data for every child in care. Where a child is at risk of
			exclusion, we expect to be involved before a decision is made, so that support can be put in
			place instead.
		</p>

		<h2>Post-16 and care leavers</h2>
		<p>
			Education support does not stop at 16. We work with personal advisers on pathways into
			college, apprenticeships, training and work, and on the financial support available to care
			leavers.
		</p>

		<h2>Training</h2>
		<p>
			We run workshops for social workers on writing and reviewing high-quality PEPs. See <a href="/training-events/">training and events</a> to book.
		</p>
	</Prose>

	<AudienceAside slot="aside" />
</AudienceLanding>
